# A source on a new line after `take`, which takes no list: `;` stays certain.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | take 5
u | count
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..21
  PIPELINE@0..10
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    TAKE_OP@4..10
      IDENT@4..8 "take"
      WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
      LITERAL@9..10
        LONG@9..10 "5"
  WHITESPACE@10..11 "\n"
  PIPELINE@11..20
    NAME_REF@11..12
      IDENT@11..12 "u"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    COUNT_OP@15..20
      IDENT@15..20 "count"
  WHITESPACE@20..21 "\n"

error[DS0106]: missing `;` between statements
  --> query:1:11
  |
1 | t | take 5
  |           ^ expected `;` here
2 | u | count
  | - a new statement starts here
  |
  = help: end the statement with `;`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | take 5;
    u | count
which parses without errors
